Apply tag name format set in the configuration, see
Apply Tag Format\&.
.RE
.sp
.it 1 an-trap
.nr an-no-space-flag 1
.nr an-break-flag 1
.br
.ps +1
\fBApply text encoding\fR
.RS 4

.HP \w'\fBtextencoding\fR\ 'u

\fBtextencoding\fR

.PP
Apply text encoding set in the configuration, see
Apply Text Encoding\&.
.RE
.sp
.it 1 an-trap
.nr an-no-space-flag 1
.nr an-break-flag 1
.br
.ps +1
\fBRename folder\fR
.RS 4

.HP \w'\fBrenamedir\fR\ 'u

\fBrenamedir\fR
 [\fIFORMAT\fR]
 [
 | create
 | rename
 | dryrun
]
 [\fITAG\-NUMBERS\fR]

.PP
Rename or create folders from the values in the tags according to a given
\fIFORMAT\fR
(e\&.g\&.
\fB%{artist} \- %{album}\fR, see
Rename Folder), if no format is given, the format defined in the
Rename folder
dialog is used\&. The default mode is
\fBrename\fR; to create folders,
\fBcreate\fR
must be given explicitly\&. The rename actions will be performed immediately, to just see what would be done, use the
\fBdryrun\fR
option\&.
.RE
.sp
.it 1 an-trap
.nr an-no-space-flag 1
.nr an-break-flag 1
.br
