.SH "INSTALLATION"


.SS "How to obtain Kid3"


.PP
Kid3
can be found at
\m[blue]\fBhttps://kid3\&.kde\&.org\fR\m[]\&.


.SS "Requirements"


.PP
Kid3
needs
\m[blue]\fBQt(TM)\fR\m[]\&\s-2\u[25]\d\s+2\&.
\m[blue]\fBKDE\fR\m[]\&\s-2\u[26]\d\s+2
is recommended but not necessary, as
Kid3
can also be compiled as a
Qt(TM)
application\&.
Kid3
can be compiled for systems where these libraries are available,
e\&.g\&.
for GNU/Linux\(rg,
Windows\(rg
and
macOS\(rg\&. To tag Ogg/Vorbis files,
\m[blue]\fBlibogg\fR\m[]\&\s-2\u[16]\d\s+2,
\m[blue]\fBlibvorbis and libvorbisfile\fR\m[]\&\s-2\u[17]\d\s+2
are required, for FLAC files
\m[blue]\fBlibFLAC++ and libFLAC\fR\m[]\&\s-2\u[18]\d\s+2\&.
\m[blue]\fBid3lib\fR\m[]\&\s-2\u[15]\d\s+2
is used for MP3 files\&. These four formats are also supported by
\m[blue]\fBTagLib\fR\m[]\&\s-2\u[19]\d\s+2, which can also handle Opus, MPC, APE, MP2, Speex, TrueAudio, WavPack, WMA, WAV, AIFF files and tracker modules\&. To import from acoustic fingerprints,
\m[blue]\fBChromaprint\fR\m[]\&\s-2\u[21]\d\s+2
and
\m[blue]\fBlibav\fR\m[]\&\s-2\u[22]\d\s+2
are used\&.
.PP
Kid3
is available for most
Linux\(rg
distributions,
Windows\(rg
and
macOS\(rg\&. Links can be found on
\m[blue]\fBhttps://kid3\&.kde\&.org\fR\m[]\&.



.SS "Compilation and Installation"


.PP
You can compile
Kid3
with or without
KDE\&. Without
KDE,
Kid3
is a simple
Qt(TM)
application and lacks some configuration and session features\&.
.PP
For a
KDE
version, go into the top folder and type
.sp
.if n \{\
.RS 4
.\}
.nf
% \fBcmake \&.\fR
% \fBmake\fR
% \fBmake install\fR
.fi
.if n \{\
.RE
.\}
.sp

.PP
To compile for different versions of
Qt(TM)
or
KDE, set the corresponding
\fBcmake\fR
options\&.
.PP
If not all libraries are present,
Kid3
is built with reduced functionality\&. So you should take care to have all desired development packages installed\&. On the other side,
\fBcmake\fR\-options control which libraries are compiled in\&. The default is
\fB\-DWITH_TAGLIB:BOOL=ON \-DWITH_MP4V2:BOOL=OFF \-DWITH_ID3LIB:BOOL=ON \-DWITH_CHROMAPRINT:BOOL=ON \-DWITH_VORBIS:BOOL=ON \-DWITH_FLAC:BOOL=ON \fR\&. These options can be disabled using
\fBOFF\fR\&.
.PP
To build
Kid3
as a
Qt(TM)
application without
KDE, use the
\fBcmake\fR
option
\fB\-DWITH_APPS=Qt\fR\&. To build both a
KDE
and a
Qt(TM)
application, set
\fB\-DWITH_APPS="Qt;KDE"\fR\&.
.PP
To use a specific
Qt(TM)
installation, set
\fB\-DQT_QMAKE_EXECUTABLE=/path/to/qmake\fR\&.
.PP
Generation of RPM\-Packages is supported by the file
kid3\&.spec, for
Debian\(rg
Packages, run
\fBbuild\&.sh deb\fR\&.

.PP
The
Qt(TM)
application can also be compiled for
Windows\(rg
and
macOS\(rg\&. The script
build\&.sh
can be used to download and build all required libraries and create a
Kid3
package\&.



.SS "Configuration"


.PP
With
KDE, the settings are stored in
\&.config/kid3rc, the application state in
\&.local/share/kid3/kid3staterc\&. As a
Qt(TM)
application, this file is in
\&.config/Kid3/Kid3\&.conf\&. On
Windows\(rg, the configuration is stored in the registry\&. on
macOS\(rg
in a plist file\&.
.PP
The environment variable
\fIKID3_CONFIG_FILE\fR
can be used to set the path of the configuration file\&.





.SH "D\-BUS INTERFACE"


.SS "D\-Bus Examples"


.PP
On
Linux\(rg
a
D\-Bus\-interface can be used to control
Kid3
by scripts\&. Scripts can be written in any language with
D\-Bus\-bindings (e\&.g\&.
in Python) and can be added to the
User Actions
to extend the functionality of
Kid3\&.

.PP
The artist in tag 2 of the current file can be set to the value "One Hit Wonder" with the following code:



.PP
Shell
.RS 4


.sp
.if n \{\
.RS 4
.\}
.nf
dbus\-send \-\-dest=org\&.kde\&.kid3 \-\-print\-reply=literal \e
/Kid3 org\&.kde\&.Kid3\&.setFrame int32:2 string:\*(AqArtist\*(Aq \e
string:\*(AqOne Hit Wonder\*(Aq
.fi
.if n \{\
.RE
.\}
.sp

or easier with
Qt(TM)\*(Aqs
\fBqdbus\fR
(\fBqdbusviewer\fR
can be used to explore the interface in a
GUI):

.sp
.if n \{\
.RS 4
.\}
.nf
qdbus org\&.kde\&.kid3 /Kid3 setFrame 2 Artist \e
\*(AqOne Hit Wonder\*(Aq
.fi
.if n \{\
.RE
.\}
.sp

.RE
.PP
Python
.RS 4


.sp
.if n \{\
.RS 4
.\}
.nf
import dbus
kid3 = dbus\&.SessionBus()\&.get_object(
  \*(Aqorg\&.kde\&.kid3\*(Aq, \*(Aq/Kid3\*(Aq)
kid3\&.setFrame(2, \*(AqArtist\*(Aq, \*(AqOne Hit Wonder\*(Aq)
.fi
.if n \{\
.RE
.\}
.sp

.RE
.PP
Perl
.RS 4


.sp
.if n \{\
.RS 4
.\}
.nf
use Net::DBus;
$kid3 = Net::DBus\->session\->get_service(
  "org\&.kde\&.kid3")\->get_object(
  "/Kid3", "org\&.kde\&.Kid3");
$kid3\->setFrame(2, "Artist", "One Hit Wonder");
.fi
.if n \{\
.RE
.\}
.sp

.RE


